    "result_text": "All tests pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 2/2). Here's a summary of the change.\n\n## What I implemented\n\nThe identity key is now `SHA-256 hex over (normalizedTelephone + '|' + lowerEmail + '|' + soundex(lastName))`, and it's the single signal driving both duplicate (409) detection and the soft-match flag.\n\n**New / changed code:**\n\n1. **`util/Soundex.java`** (new) \u2014 standard 4-char American Soundex encoder (`\"Smith\"`/`\"Smyth\"` \u2192 `\"S530\"`), with vowel/`H`/`W` handling. Single responsibility, reused by both the identity key and the soft-match detector.\n\n2. **`util/Sha256.java`** \u2014 added `hex(String)` returning the full 64-char **lower-case** digest (the existing `hexPrefix` stays upper-case for household id / customer code). Factored the digest step into a shared private helper so both methods reuse it.\n\n3. **`model/Owner.getIdentityKey()`** \u2014 now returns `Sha256.hex(telephone + \"|\" + lowerEmail + \"|\" + Soundex.encode(lastName))` instead of the old plaintext `telephone|email|householdId` join. `householdId` no longer participates in the key.\n\n4. **`service/PossibleDuplicateDetector`** \u2014 the soft-match now fires when **identityKey differs** but **soundex(lastName) and postcode match** (previously: exact last name + postcode + different telephone). Because telephone is folded into the key, two owners with the same last name/postcode but different phones now surface here as a soft match rather than a hard 409.\n\n5. **Duplicate detection** \u2014 `ClinicServiceImpl.isIdentityDuplicate` is unchanged in shape and remains the *single* duplicate check (409), still narrowing by telephone \u2014 valid since normalizedTelephone is part of the key \u2014 still ignoring `deleted` owners, and the controller still applies the email-domain blocklist first. There was no separate householdId-based 409 block to remove; the single identity-key check is now the only one.\n\n6. **Docs** \u2014 updated the stale key-composition descriptions in `ClinicService`, `DuplicateIdentityException`, `ExceptionControllerAdvice`, and `openapi.yml` (`identityKey` description/example \u2192 64-char lower-case digest).\n\nThe two acceptance checks \u2014 `identityKey` matching `[0-9a-f]{64}`, and an identical telephone/email/lastName copy returning 409 \u2014 both pass.",
